From: Flint 4 build CI
Subject: mediatek: filogic: GL-BE14000: leave the panel SPI bus widths at default

The panel node in mainline sets spi-tx-bus-width = <1> and
spi-rx-bus-width = <0>. JiaY-shi's tree spelled these spi-tx-buswidth and
spi-rx-buswidth, so the kernel never saw them and the SPI core used its
defaults - and on that tree the panel lights up with the stock GL.iNet
U-Boot. On mainline it is reported to stay dark with the stock U-Boot.
These two properties are the only difference in the panel node between
the two trees, so drop them to match the configuration known to work.

--- a/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7988a-glinet-gl-be14000.dts
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7988a-glinet-gl-be14000.dts
@@ -673,8 +673,6 @@
 		compatible = "glinet,gl-be14000-panel", "panel-mipi-dbi-spi";
 		reg = <0>;
 		spi-max-frequency = <52000000>;
-		spi-tx-bus-width = <1>;
-		spi-rx-bus-width = <0>;
 		spi-cpol;
 		spi-cpha;
 
